I agree it is unlikely to work, and urge that it's probably
not worth your trouble, for which I make the following
arguments.

1) There is a class of players, mine, who would only ever
upload patsy bonefiles because except by grotesque mischance
we don't survive long enough to encounter real nasties.

2) There is a class of players at the other end (you can
spot them by the lists in their siggies so they can remember
which roles they _haven't_ ascended yet, you know who you
are), who except by grotesque mischance aren't going to be
creating bones files that don't contain immense problems for
whatever an "average" Nethack player might be.

3) There is a class of "merciful" uploaders cleverly
imitating class #1.

4) There is a class of "sadistic" uploaders cleverly
imitating class #2.

5) There is a class of uploaders doing what you want them to
do, and there's frankly no protection against people that
clever. <grin>

You'd have about as much chance figuring out who was who
between #1 and #3 or #2 and #4, from the evidence at your
end, as of developing meaningful golf or bowling
handicaps, and those systems are rife with cheating as it
is.

I'd just go with hoping #3s and #4s either balance out or
give up the game soon because they aren't that into the game
culture anyway and finally lose interest.

